{
  "schemaVersion": 4,
  "id": "t02-010",
  "track": "track-02",
  "title": "HTTP request response headers forms files and streaming bodies",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "inventoryComplete": true,
  "concepts": [
    "HttpRequest and HttpResponse are per-request abstractions exposed through HttpContext. Headers and status can be changed only until the response starts; once bytes are committed, error handling and late metadata changes have different constraints.",
    "Request bodies are one-way streams by default. Reading consumes bytes; EnableBuffering permits rereading within configured thresholds and limits but has memory and temporary-disk costs. Prefer bounded streaming for large payloads.",
    "ASP.NET Core exposes stream and pipeline views of request and response bodies. PipeReader and PipeWriter support lower-allocation incremental processing, but callers must correctly advance and flush buffers and respect cancellation and completion rules.",
    "Form model binding buffers uploaded files by default. Buffered IFormFile is convenient for small bounded uploads; MultipartReader streams multipart sections for large inputs. Enforce size limits, validate content, use server-generated storage names, and never trust a client filename or content-type claim."
  ],
