  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": "ASP.NET Core 11 / .NET 11 GA checked 2026-11-14",
      "items": [
        "From .NET 10, Minimal API JSON body binding, MVC JSON input formatters, and HttpRequest JSON helpers use PipeReader-based JsonSerializer.DeserializeAsync overloads by default. Apps with converters that mishandle Utf8JsonReader.HasValueSequence can temporarily opt back into stream-based parsing with Microsoft.AspNetCore.UseStreamBasedJsonParsing; fix converters rather than relying on the compatibility switch long term.",
        "File upload guidance continues to distinguish buffering for smaller uploads from streaming for large uploads. Do not teach the memory threshold or multipart limit as a security guarantee; application, server, proxy, and storage limits must be considered together."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/fundamentals/minimal-apis",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/mvc/models/file-uploads"
      ]
    }
